  "notes": "A bat seen from below, head up the V0-V3 diagonal. Ears either side of V3; wingtips at V1 and V5 (each pokes into the notch between a neighbour's ears); wrists at the 3-fold centres V2 and V4; tail membrane at V0. The hand wing's leading edge (e1) is the arm's edge (e2) turned a third about the wrist, so the ear makes the notch by the wingtip. e4 is e2 with v negated, so head and arms are mirror-symmetric. The trailing edge e0 is scalloped between the foot and the finger tips; its turned copy e5 shows the same scallops inverted on the left wing.",
